WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.072 --> 00:00:05.855
- I'm Eric Mason, I'm a mother,
and I'm a transgender guy.

00:00:05.855 --> 00:00:08.755
Corey is my 15-year-old
transgender daughter.

00:00:08.755 --> 00:00:10.740
I started transitioning
almost two years ago,

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:14.342
and Corey started transitioning
almost five years ago.

00:00:14.342 --> 00:00:16.029
- I've always known that I was different.

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:17.836
I've always known that

00:00:17.836 --> 00:00:19.753
I'm not the “normal” boy.

00:00:21.089 --> 00:00:23.218
I was never like,

00:00:23.218 --> 00:00:25.869
happy, I was always negative.

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:30.036
When I first put on some make
up, I was like... wow ...(gasping)

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:38.173
- My family is made up of me, my husband,

00:00:38.173 --> 00:00:39.923
and my five children.

00:00:41.325 --> 00:00:42.158
I waited, um,

00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:46.903
until Corey was completely
through her transition

00:00:46.903 --> 00:00:47.736
before I, I,

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.223
came out myself.

00:00:51.862 --> 00:00:54.438
It was really hard keeping that secret

00:00:54.438 --> 00:00:57.660
from my family, especially
from my husband.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.146
But, at the time I just knew
I had to focus on my child.

00:01:02.146 --> 00:01:04.921
- I've been bullied since fifth grade and

00:01:04.921 --> 00:01:07.588
still getting bullied sometimes.

00:01:08.606 --> 00:01:12.773
When kids said I should go
and kill myself, because

00:01:13.684 --> 00:01:15.017
I was different,

00:01:16.863 --> 00:01:19.863
(crying) I'm sorry.

00:01:21.962 --> 00:01:26.129
When my mom came out I was
like, I'm not alone anymore.

00:01:27.001 --> 00:01:29.356
We can actually understand
what we're going through

00:01:29.356 --> 00:01:31.975
with each other, we can, you know, talk to each other

00:01:31.975 --> 00:01:34.942
if we're having a bad day.

00:01:34.942 --> 00:01:36.783
- Me supporting Corey

00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:38.979
is, in my opinion,

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:41.872
what you're supposed to do as a parent.

00:01:41.872 --> 00:01:44.874
You're supposed to support
your children no matter what.

00:01:44.874 --> 00:01:47.589
So I don't feel like I did
anything special, I didn't.

00:01:47.589 --> 00:01:49.389
I just love my kid.

00:01:49.389 --> 00:01:51.319
I love my kid no matter
what she looks like,

00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:53.515
no matter who she wants to be.

00:01:53.515 --> 00:01:55.099
We are stronger as a family.

00:01:55.099 --> 00:01:57.863
I think any time you are
living your authentic self

00:01:57.863 --> 00:01:59.528
and you are living your truth,

00:01:59.528 --> 00:02:01.200
it makes you a better person overall,

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.441
it makes you a better parent,

00:02:02.441 --> 00:02:04.203
it makes you a better spouse.

00:02:04.203 --> 00:02:05.203
My family is

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.087
everything.

00:02:08.273 --> 00:02:09.561
We

00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:13.145
fight, we laugh, we cry,
we're a typical family.

00:02:13.145 --> 00:02:14.702
We just look a little different.

00:02:14.702 --> 00:02:15.914
That's it!

00:02:15.914 --> 00:02:18.247
That's all it boils down to.

